# Audit finding #5. Hawa develops on Windows, where the Git installer's default is
# core.autocrlf=true. Without this, `scripts/verify.sh` is checked out with CRLF and bash
# dies on line 7 — `set -euo pipefail\r` is not an option name. A gate that cannot start
# cannot refuse anything, so the line endings of the gate are a correctness property.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
scripts/test-count.floor text eol=lf
# `git archive` is a release input.  On Windows with core.autocrlf=true, an unpinned
# text member is exported with CRLF even when the committed blob is LF.  Dependency
# locks are authenticated by their committed SHA-256, so byte identity is mandatory.
*.txt text eol=lf
# models/sources.json is tracked (see .gitignore) and read on both platforms; §5's clip
# documents and every fixture are JSON too. One line ending, so a checkout on Windows and a
# checkout on the CI runner hash the same bytes.
*.json text eol=lf

# Binary evidence: the golden caption render is compared pixel by pixel (§4.3.6). Any
# newline translation would corrupt it into a test failure with a baffling diff.
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
*.wav binary
*.mp4 binary
